# Frontend Development Rules

Follow the existing frontend architecture.

Reuse existing components whenever possible.

Never create new components without approval.

Never duplicate UI logic.

Never duplicate CSS.

Reuse existing styles.

Maintain consistency across the application.

Keep components simple.

Avoid unnecessary complexity.

Keep state management consistent.

Never redesign unrelated pages.

Never change routing without approval.

Never introduce new frontend libraries without approval.

Always ensure responsive layouts.

Always consider accessibility.

Keep interactions predictable.

Do not introduce unnecessary animations.

Respect the existing design language.